                                         <widget class="HelpIconLabel" name="label_58">
                                                                           <property name="toolTip">
                                                                            <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head/&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=" font-weight:700;"&gt;Pixel Format&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- D&lt;span style=" font-family:'Droid Sans Mono','monospace','monospace'; font-size:9pt; color:#cccccc;"&gt;efines how color information is stored for each pixel in a video frame.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=" font-family:'Droid Sans Mono','monospace','monospace'; font-size:9pt; color:#cccccc;"&gt;- yuv420p: Most common, removes the most information. &lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=" font-weight:700;"&gt;mkv, mp4, mov, avi, webm&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=" font-family:'Droid Sans Mono','monospace','monospace'; font-size:9pt; color:#cccccc;"&gt;- yuv422p: In between 420p and 444p. &lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=" font-weight:700;"&gt;mkv, mov, mp4&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=" font-family:'Droid Sans Mono','monospace','monospace'; font-size:9pt; color:#cccccc;"&gt;- yuv444p: Keeps the most information. &lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=" font-weight:700;"&gt;mkv, mov, mp4&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- &lt;span style=" font-family:'Droid Sans Mono','monospace','monospace'; font-size:9pt; color:#cccccc;"&gt;yuv 420/422/444 p10le: 10 bit version of each. (MKV and MP4 containers only) &lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=" font-weight:700;"&gt;mkv, mov, mp4&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
                                                                           </property>
